10 ' Sound effect board. Press 1-9 for an effect, 0 for an engine, Q to quit.
20 SFX 1,"W1 ML S3000,200,8"
30 SFX 2,"W3 V1 ML X0,0.02,0.4,0.5 S1200,40,2"
40 SFX 3,"W2 ML ~6,0.5 S300,1800,4"
50 SFX 4,"W1 V0.35 ML X0,0.3,0,0.05 H988,16 H1319,4"
60 SFX 5,"W1 ML S200,600,16"
70 SFX 6,"W2 V0.5 ML S500,900,4 S900,500,4 S500,900,4 S900,500,4"
80 SFX 7,"W1 V0.4 ML H880,16 R16 H880,16 R16 H880,16"
90 SFX 8,"W1 ML S2500,300,16 S2500,300,16 S2500,300,16"
100 SFX 9,"W3 V0.8 ML X0,0.05,0,0.01 H300,16 R8 H250,16 R8 H300,16 R8 H250,16"
110 PRINT "SOUND EFFECTS"
120 PRINT "1 laser        6 siren"
130 PRINT "2 explosion    7 alarm"
140 PRINT "3 power-up     8 laser burst"
150 PRINT "4 coin         9 footsteps"
160 PRINT "5 jump         0 engine"
170 PRINT "Q quit"
180 GET K$
190 IF K$="Q" OR K$="q" THEN SOUND OFF:END
200 IF K$="0" THEN GOSUB 500:GOTO 180
210 K=VAL(K$)
220 IF K>=1 AND K<=9 THEN SFX K
230 GOTO 180
500 ' Engine: a tone without an end, then PITCH and VOLUME change it while it runs.
505 ' Channel 8 is also the one SFX picks when the others are busy, and an effect leaves its envelope behind: start clean.
506 SOUND OFF 8:ENVELOPE 8:TREMOLO 8,0,0
510 WAVE 8,1:VIBRATO 8,14,0.25
520 SOUND 8,50,0,0.3
530 FOR I=0 TO 100
540 PITCH 8,50+I*2.5
550 VOLUME 8,0.3+I/250
560 WAIT 2
570 NEXT I
580 FOR I=100 TO 0 STEP -1
590 PITCH 8,50+I*2.5
600 VOLUME 8,0.3+I/250
610 WAIT 2
620 NEXT I
630 SOUND OFF 8
640 VIBRATO 8,0,0:WAVE 8,0
650 RETURN
